NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q0P651","text":"Catalyzes the hydrolysis of an acyl chain from the tetra-acylated cardiolipin (CL) and produces the tri-acylated monolysocardiolipin (MLCL) (PubMed:40903572). Prefers CL with shorter and saturated fatty acyl chains as substrates (PubMed:40903572). Together with Tafazzin (TAZ), it participates in the mechanism of CL remodeling, a process consisting of repetitive cycles of hydrolysis and reacylation of the fatty acids that make up CL, where the nascent acyl chains are replaced with longer, unsaturated chains (PubMed:40903572)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}